untry></address></addressbook></applicant> <applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SAKAI KOKKI</name> <address><country>JP</country> </address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>WAKAO CONSTRUCTION CO LTD</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>WAKAO KOICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>BIO REMEDIATION TECHNOROGIE, INC.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KONDO, RYUICHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAKAI, KOKKI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>WAKAO CONSTRUCTION CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>WAKAO, KOICHI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KONDO RYUICHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SAKAI KOKKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>WAKAO KOICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KONDO, RYUICHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAKAI, KOKKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>WAKAO, KOICHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A white rot fungus is screened from rotten wood and a strain MZ-340 is thus isolated. This strain MZ-340 can be cultured in Kirk's liquid medium (HCLN) or a PDB medium. By using this strain MZ-340, a novel system for degrading dioxins in incineration ash is constructed. Thus, dioxins in the incineration ash can be effectively and efficiently degraded both in liquid and solid phase systems. As a result, environmental pollution caused by dioxins evolving via incineration can be prevented and materials contaminated with dioxins can be cleaned up.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>On crible un champignon des charpentes blanc à partir de bois putréfié et on isole ainsi une souche de MZ-340. Cette souche de MZ-340 peut être cultivée dans le milieu liquide de Kirk (HCLN) ou dans un milieu PDB. Avec cette souche, on met au point un nouveau système de dégradation de dioxines dans la cendre d'incinération. Ainsi, on peut dégrader de façon effective et efficace les dioxines se trouvant dans la cendre d'incinération dans des systèmes en phase solide et liquide. Par conséquent, on peut empêcher la pollution de l'environnement provoquée par les dioxines provenant d'une incinération et on peut nettoyer le matériel contaminé par des dioxines.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>